      "message": "awesome, that sounds great, if it is possible to proceed :) \n\n\nissue: https://issues.gerritcodereview.com/issues/514979798\n\nScreenshots are attached to the bug.\n\nThe reason we can\u0027t just reuse the existing commit linkify/weblinks is that those resolve to gitiles (or whatever gitweb is configured to). For Chromium, the existing weblink for a commit SHA would point to:\n\n  https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/\u003csha\u003e (gitiles)\n\nBut what i actually would love is:\n\n  https://chromiumdash.appspot.com/commit/\u003csha\u003e (ChromiumDash)\n\nChromiumDash shows usefull info in what milestone the CL landed (https://chromiumdash.appspot.com/commit/a266895e21e455b6101e834d1780d526aab67fdd)\n\nthats the reason for `gerrit.submitCommitUrl` as a new config option it falls back to deriving a URL from the existing revision weblinks.",
