      "side": 1,
      "message": "A few minor edge cases and safety considerations:\n\n1. **Trailing slash handling**: If an administrator sets `gerrit.submitCommitUrl \u003d https://chromiumdash.appspot.com/commit` without a trailing `/`, direct concatenation produces `https://chromiumdash.appspot.com/commitabcdef...` (a broken URL). We should ensure `commitUrl` is normalized to end with a `/` or supports a `{commit}` placeholder.\n2. **URL protocol check**: We should ensure the configured URL starts with `http://` or `https://` to avoid unintended URL schemes.\n3. **Commit Hash Scope**: The global `/([0-9a-f]{40})/g` regex will match any 40-char hex string in the message (e.g. tree IDs or plugin metadata). Scoping the match to the standard submit phrase pattern (e.g. matching after \u0027merged as commit\u0027 or \u0027as commit\u0027) could prevent unintended replacements.",
